 "details": [
  "Climate scenarios used were from the NEX-GDDP-CMIP6 dataset, prepared by the Climate Analytics Group and NASA Ames Research Center using the NASA Earth eXchange (NEX) and distributed by the NASA Center for Climate Simulation (NCCS).",
  "NASA's own words on use: “This dataset is intended for use in scientific research only, and use of this dataset for other purposes, such as commercial applications, and engineering or design studies is not recommended without consultation with a qualified expert.”",
  "Seven global models: ACCESS-ESM1-5, CNRM-ESM2-1, EC-Earth3, GFDL-ESM4, GISS-E2-1-G, MIROC6, and MRI-ESM2-0. An eighth planned model, MPI-ESM1-2-HR, was left out to fit a download cap.",
  "At 2040 to 2059 the two scenarios barely differ, and in some counties the higher-emissions median is the cooler of the two.",
  "Each county's figure is the plain mean of the grid cells whose centres fall inside it, after each cell's own count or mean is taken. Checked against NOAA's 1991 to 2020 station normals in two counties, the 1995 to 2014 daytime highs ran warmer than the station, and precipitation ran drier in one county and wetter in the other."
 ],
 "foot": [
  {
   "text": "Every county, measure, and scenario, with each model's own figure.",
   "href": "../data/climate-regions.json",
